## 6. Remaining target

Before this run, the still-open low-symmetry `(2,2,2,2)` support geometries consisted of

```text
stabilizer order 1:  2 orbits
stabilizer order 2:  8 orbits
stabilizer order 4: 11 orbits
stabilizer order 6:  2 orbits
```

The two order-6 orbits are now closed. The remaining `(2,2,2,2)` support geometries are therefore

```text
2 + 8 + 11 = 21 support-set orbits,
```

all of stabilizer order `1`, `2`, or `4`.

The full `(3,2,2,1)` profile also remains open on its support-nullity-four geometries. The direct next target is the same completion-independent external-rank-increment test, preferably on another bounded low-symmetry shard.

The other unresolved `k=5` arithmetic branches remain

```text
D=-2, (d_root,p)=(0,5),
D=-1, (d_root,p)=(0,6).
```

No theorem-state authority file is changed by this note.